---
/*
 * ============================================================================
 * src/pages/admin/write.astro  —  the admin-only writing surface (the dashboard's "Write")
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * WHAT THIS FILE IS / SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY
 * -----------------------------------------
 * The full in-browser authoring experience for the blog: a Medium-style
 * WYSIWYG editor plus the "Publish" flow that turns what you wrote into a
 * committed Markdown post. It is one Astro page — statically built like every
 * other route, but essentially a client-side app (all the logic lives in the
 * bottom <script>, which Astro bundles/transpiles). The page renders nothing
 * meaningful server-side beyond an empty shell + a hidden publish modal.
 *
 * WHERE IT SITS IN THE ARCHITECTURE
 * ---------------------------------
 * Stack: static Astro build hosted on Cloudflare Pages, with Pages Functions
 * (functions/api/*) for the few dynamic bits, Supabase for auth + data, and
 * Dodo for payments/premium (this page touches only auth + publish; it does
 * not talk to Dodo directly). Data flow when you hit Publish (ONE path — into the DB):
 *
 *   write.astro (this file)                      ← author writes, gets Markdown; the
 *        │                                          browser renders body_html in-page
 *        │  POST /api/author/post    { slug, title, body_md, body_html, … } + JWT
 *        │  POST /api/author/publish { post_id, body_html, … }               + JWT
 *        ▼
 *   functions/api/author/*.js (Pages Functions)  ← requireAuthor, then service-role RPCs
 *        │  author_save_post → content.posts (draft)     assertInert(body_html) then
 *        │  author_publish   → content.publish_post       commits status='published'
 *        ▼
 *   /@handle/slug  goes live INSTANTLY — the reader edge middleware serves body_html
 *   from content.posts via get_public_post. No file, no GitHub commit, no rebuild.
 *
 * So this page never writes files or repo state; it renders body_html in the browser
 * (the pipeline sanitises mid-render) and hands { body_md, body_html } + the user's JWT
 * to the gated Function, which is the trusted boundary (a light inert-guard backstops
 * the submitted HTML). The reader renders the SAME fenced code (```d2, ```python) so
 * editor preview == live. Every post has exactly ONE canonical URL: /@handle/slug.
 *
 * KEY IMPORTS / DEPENDENCIES (see the <script> import block for the full list)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *   - @milkdown/crepe                 the WYSIWYG editor ("Crepe" preset), Markdown-native
 *   - @milkdown/kit/prose/*           ProseMirror internals (Plugin/Decoration/…) for our
 *                                     two custom plugins: bracket auto-pairing + Plotly cells
 *   - @codemirror/language-data + /autocomplete   language-aware code blocks, close-brackets
 *   - @terrastruct/d2                 D2 diagram engine (WASM), lazy-loaded for ```d2 preview
 *   - ../../lib/plotly                runs author ```python via Pyodide + renders with plotly.js,
 *                                     plus makeRotatingGif() for 3D-figure GIF export
 *   - ../../lib/supabase             browser Supabase client (session, OAuth, magic-link, JWT)
 *   - ../../lib/admin-gate           whenAdmin/cachedAdmin — boot the editor only for an admin
 *   - ../../layouts/AdminLayout.astro dashboard shell + client access gate
 * WHAT DEPENDS ON THIS FILE: nothing imports it (it is a leaf route). It is the
 * sole producer of requests to functions/api/author/{post,publish}.js.
 *
 * IMPORTANT DESIGN DECISIONS / NON-OBVIOUS GOTCHAS
 * ------------------------------------------------
 *   - Markdown-native by design (Option B): Crepe serialises straight to the .md
 *     format the content collection consumes — no HTML round-trip, no lossy AST.
 *   - D2 REPLACED Mermaid. Diagrams are authored in ```d2 fences and previewed
 *     client-side via @terrastruct/d2 (see renderPreview below); the old Milkdown
 *     Mermaid plugin is gone. If you find "mermaid" anywhere, it is stale.
 *   - Interactive ```python plots are NOT drawn by Crepe's sanitised code-block
 *     preview. They are a separate ProseMirror WIDGET decoration (plotlyCells)
 *     injected just after each python block, so Plotly's interactivity/DOM
 *     survives Crepe's sanitiser. See the long comment on that plugin.
 *   - Two hand-rolled ProseMirror plugins are wired via crepe.editor.use():
 *     bracketPairing (auto-pair brackets/quotes in prose) and plotlyCells.
 *   - Draft autosave is localStorage-only for now (key 'aysr:editor-draft'),
 *     debounced; there is no server-side draft store yet (see the TODO).
 *   - The Publish modal is a two-state premium flow: sign-in view → metadata
 *     form. Frontmatter is built by hand and the leading "# Title" is stripped
 *     from the body to avoid a duplicate <h1> (title comes from frontmatter).
 *
 * SECURITY / CORRECTNESS CAVEATS  (READ BEFORE SHIPPING)
 * ------------------------------------------------------
 *   - ACCESS: this page renders inside AdminLayout, whose client gate reveals the
 *     /admin shell only for a confirmed admin; the editor here boots via
 *     whenAdmin/cachedAdmin (bottom of the script), so init() runs only for an admin.
 *     That gate is UX only. The REAL protection is server-side: functions/api/publish.js
 *     (and /api/admin/*) re-verify is_admin via lib/require-admin.js before committing
 *     anything, so a non-admin who forced the UI open still cannot ship.
 *   - Publish auth rides on the Supabase access_token sent as a Bearer header;
 *     the Function trusts that token, not the client's claims.
 *   - Frontmatter scalars are emitted via JSON.stringify (yaml() helper) because
 *     a JSON string literal is also a valid YAML scalar — this is the injection
 *     guard for user-supplied title/description/tags.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import AdminLayout from '../../layouts/AdminLayout.astro';
---

<AdminLayout title="Write — Studio" heading="Write" active="write">
  <div id="editor-wrap">
    <div class="wtop">
      <span class="badge" id="w-state">Draft</span>
      <div class="sess">
        <span><b id="w-words">0</b> words</span>
        <span>est. <b id="w-read">0 min</b></span>
        <span class="goalwrap" id="w-goalwrap" hidden><span class="goal"><i id="w-goalbar" style="width:0%"></i></span><span id="w-goaltext"></span></span>
        <span id="w-today-wrap"><b id="w-today">0</b> today</span>
        <span id="w-streak" hidden></span>
        <span id="editor-status" class="muted"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="acts">
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="new-draft" type="button">New</button>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="focusbtn" type="button">Focus</button>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="get-md" type="button">Preview</button>
        <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="publish-btn" type="button">Publish…</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="publish-modal" class="pm-overlay" hidden>
      {/* Sign-in view (a small card) */}
      <div id="pm-signin" class="pm-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Sign in to publish" hidden>
        <h2 class="pm-title">Sign in to publish</h2>
        <p class="pm-sub">Your draft is saved on this device. Sign in once to publish it to the world.</p>
        <button class="pm-btn pm-btn-primary" id="pm-github" type="button">Continue with GitHub</button>
        <div class="pm-or">or</div>
        <form id="pm-magic" class="pm-magic">
          <input id="pm-email" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required />
          <button class="pm-btn" type="submit">Email me a link</button>
        </form>
        <p class="pm-status" id="pm-signin-status"></p>
      </div>

      {/* Press-check sheet — built to editorial/studio.css exactly. The publish ENGINE
          is unchanged: every input ID is the one the #pm-publish handler reads; #pm-draft
          is a hidden flag the footer buttons set. Scheduling + members-only aren't in our
          backend, so those are disabled/omitted (not faked). */}
      <div id="pm-form" class="sh" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Publish" hidden>
        <header class="shhead">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Press check</span>
            <h2 id="pm-form-title">Ready to publish</h2>
            <div class="shsub" id="ps-sub"></div>
          </div>
          <button class="shx" id="pm-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
        </header>

        <div class="shbody">
          <div class="shcol">
            <div>
              <div class="dl">Who can read it</div>
              <div class="pick" id="accpick">
                <button class="pk on" type="button" data-a="free"><span class="rd"></span><span><b>Free</b><small>Anyone, no account.</small></span></button>
                <button class="pk" type="button" data-a="paid"><span class="rd"></span><span><b>Paid</b><small>A teaser shows; readers pay what they want to unlock the rest.</small></span></button>
              </div>
              <div class="sub-x off" id="pricebox">
                <div class="para"><span>Suggested price</span><span>$<input id="pm-price" class="pin" type="number" min="0" step="0.5" value="5" aria-label="Suggested price"></span><span>readers can pay more</span></div>
                <div style="margin-top:6px;color:var(--ink-faint)">Add a <b>Paywall</b> block in the editor to place the cut; you can change all this on Posts.</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <div class="dl">When</div>
              <div class="pick" id="whenpick">
                <button class="pk on" type="button" data-w="now"><span class="rd"></span><span><b>Publish now</b><small>Live in a few seconds.</small></span></button>
                <button class="pk" type="button" data-w="later"><span class="rd"></span><span><b>Schedule it</b><small>Goes live on its own at a time you pick.</small></span></button>
              </div>
              <div class="sub-x off" id="schedbox">
                <div class="sched">
                  <div class="spwrap" id="spw-date">
                    <button type="button" class="spick" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Publish date">
                      <svg class="spick-i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><rect x="3" y="4.5" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M8 2.5v4M16 2.5v4"/></svg>
                      <span class="spick-v" id="sp-date-v">Pick a date</span>
                    </button>
                    <div class="spop" role="dialog" hidden></div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spwrap" id="spw-time">
                    <button type="button" class="spick" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Publish time">
                      <svg class="spick-i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7.5V12l3 2"/></svg>
                      <span class="spick-v" id="sp-time-v">Set time</span>
                    </button>
                    <div class="spop" role="dialog" hidden></div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spwrap spwrap-tz" id="spw-tz">
                    <button type="button" class="spick" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Time zone">
                      <svg class="spick-i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.5 2.5 15 0 18M12 3c-2.5 2.5-2.5 15 0 18"/></svg>
                      <span class="spick-v" id="sp-tz-v">Time zone</span>
                      <svg class="spick-c" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
                    </button>
                    <div class="spop" role="listbox" hidden></div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <input type="hidden" id="pm-sched-date" />
                <input type="hidden" id="pm-sched-time" />
                <input type="hidden" id="pm-sched-tz" />
                <div id="pm-sched-note" style="margin-top:8px;color:var(--ink-faint)">Saved hidden until then; a cron publishes it (within ~15 min of the time).</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <div class="dl">Who gets told</div>
              <div class="mailrow">
                <span class="who" id="pm-email-subs-label">Send with the letter</span>
                <button class="tog" id="pm-mail-tog" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Send with the letter"></button>
              </div>
              <div class="subj"><input id="pm-subject" aria-label="Subject line" placeholder="Subject line — defaults to the title"></div>
              <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-faint);margin-top:7px">Free readers get up to the cut; paid readers get the whole thing. One-click unsubscribe in every email.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="shcol">
            <div>
              <div class="dl">Before it goes</div>
              <ul class="chk" id="ps-checklist"><li>Checking…</li></ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="dl">What readers will see</div>
              <div class="rec">
                <div class="rr"><span class="k">Title</span><span class="v"><input id="pm-post-title" class="recin" placeholder="Your title" /></span></div>
                <div class="rr"><span class="k">Standfirst</span><span class="v"><textarea id="pm-post-desc" class="recin" rows="2" placeholder="One sentence that makes people want to read."></textarea></span></div>
                <div class="rr"><span class="k">Tags</span><span class="v"><div class="pm-tags chips" id="pm-tags"><input id="pm-tag-input" class="recin" placeholder="Add a tag…" style="width:auto;flex:1;min-width:80px" /></div></span></div>
                <div class="rr"><span class="k">Series</span><span class="v">
                  <span style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
                    <span id="pm-series-pick" style="flex:1;min-width:150px"></span>
                    <input id="pm-series-order" class="recin" type="text" inputmode="numeric" maxlength="3" placeholder="Part" style="width:54px;text-align:center" aria-label="Part number" />
                    <button type="button" class="specsbtn off" id="pm-series-more" aria-expanded="false" title="Series details for the plate"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
                  </span>
                  <input type="hidden" id="pm-series" />
                </span></div>
                <div class="rr"><span class="k">Address</span><span class="v slug"><i>areyoustillreading.dev/blog/</i><span id="pm-slug" class="pm-slug" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false"></span></span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sub-x off" id="seriesknobs">
                <div class="knob-h">On the series plate</div>
                <div class="fr"><span>Parts planned</span><span class="v"><input id="pm-series-total" class="pin" type="number" min="1" placeholder="—" aria-label="Planned total parts" title="Total planned parts — drives “3 of 5” + the Complete badge" /></span></div>
                <div class="fr"><span>Status</span><span class="v"><select id="pm-series-status" class="sel" aria-label="Series status" style="width:auto;min-width:132px">
                  <option value="">Auto</option>
                  <option value="in-progress">In progress</option>
                  <option value="complete">Complete</option>
                  <option value="paused">Paused</option>
                </select></span></div>
                <div style="margin-top:11px">
                  <div class="knob-l">Parts still to come</div>
                  <textarea id="pm-series-planned" rows="2" placeholder="One title per line — shown greyed on the series page"></textarea>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <footer class="shfoot">
          <span class="shnote" id="ps-note"></span>
          <span class="shacts pm-actions">
            <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="pm-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button>
            <button class="btn btn-sm" id="pm-save-draft" type="button" title="Save as a hidden draft — only you can see it, not emailed">Save as draft</button>
            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="pm-publish" type="button">Publish now</button>
            <span class="pm-progress" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="pm-status" id="pm-form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
          </span>
        </footer>
        {/* Hidden flags/inputs read by the unchanged engine: draft (footer buttons set it),
            email opt-in (the mail toggle drives it). */}
        <input id="pm-draft" type="checkbox" hidden />
        <input id="pm-email-subs" type="checkbox" hidden />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wr">
      <div class="wcanvas">
        <div id="milkdown"></div>
        <pre id="md-out" hidden></pre>
      </div>
      <aside class="rail" id="wrail">
        <div class="railtabs" id="rtabs">
          <button class="on" data-p="outline" type="button">Outline</button>
          <button data-p="notes" type="button">Notes</button>
          <button data-p="post" type="button">Post</button>
        </div>
        <div class="rpane on" data-pane="outline">
          <div class="grp"><ul class="olist" id="r-outline"><li class="rempty">Headings appear here as you write.</li></ul></div>
          <div class="grp rnote">Each heading becomes a section on the published page. Reading time sets this post's height on the <a href="/series/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">series</a> plate.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rpane" data-pane="notes">
          <div class="grp"><ul class="nlist" id="r-notes"><li class="rempty">No notes yet. These stay private — never published.</li></ul></div>
          <div class="grp"><input class="input" id="r-note-input" placeholder="Add a note — stays private" autocomplete="off" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="rpane" data-pane="post">
          <div class="grp">
            <div class="gl">Length target</div>
            <div class="fr"><span>Target</span><span class="v"><input id="r-target" class="input inp-mini" type="number" min="0" step="100" placeholder="—" aria-label="Word target" /></span></div>
            <div class="fr"><span>Written</span><span class="v act" id="r-written">0</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="grp">
            <div class="gl">This post</div>
            <div class="fr"><span>Series</span><span class="v" id="r-series">None</span></div>
            <div class="fr"><span>State</span><span class="v" id="r-state2">Draft</span></div>
            <div class="fr"><span>Saved</span><span class="v act" id="r-saved">—</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="grp"><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="r-openpub" type="button" style="width:100%">Publishing options…</button></div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="wstatus">
      <span id="w-statusline">0 words · 0 min read</span>
      <span class="r"><kbd>/</kbd> blocks &nbsp; <kbd>⌘\</kbd> focus &nbsp; <kbd>⌘⏎</kbd> publish</span>
    </div>
    <div class="esc" id="w-esc" hidden>Focus mode — <kbd>Esc</kbd> to come back</div>
  </div>
</AdminLayout>

<style>
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  /* Write chrome (.wtop / .wr / .rail / .railtabs / .rpane / .wstatus / focus)
     lives in global admin.css — the Outline/Notes lists are injected via
     innerHTML, which Astro's scoped styles can't reach. */
  #milkdown {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; min-height: 60vh;
    background: var(--bg); overflow: hidden;
  }
  #md-out {
    margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px; background: var(--code-bg); overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  /* The `hidden` attribute MUST win. Without this, the `.pm-overlay { display:flex }`
     rule below (author origin) overrides the UA `[hidden] { display:none }`, so the
     modal stays permanently rendered — an empty overlay covering the editor with a
     close button that appears dead (closeModal sets `hidden`, which display:flex
     ignores). This attribute-qualified selector has higher specificity, restoring it. */
  .pm-overlay[hidden] { display: none; }
  .pm-overlay {
    position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 100; display: flex; align-items: center;
    justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; background: rgba(12, 14, 18, 0.55);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px); animation: pm-fade 0.15s ease;
  }
  @keyframes pm-fade { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
  @keyframes pm-pop { from { transform: translateY(10px) scale(0.98); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
  .pm-card {
    position: relative; width: 100%; max-width: 46rem; background: var(--bg); color: inherit;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.75rem 1.9rem 1.4rem;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); animation: pm-pop 0.18s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
    max-height: 92vh; overflow-y: auto;
  }
  #pm-signin { max-width: 26rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .pm-close {
    position: absolute; top: 0.85rem; right: 1rem; border: 0; background: transparent;
    color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.7rem; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; padding: 0;
  }
  .pm-title { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.45rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pm-sub { margin: 0 0 1.35rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pm-field { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pm-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.07em; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-card input[type="text"], .pm-card input[type="email"], .pm-card input[type="number"], .pm-card textarea {
    width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font: inherit; color: var(--fg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius-sm); background: var(--surface);
  }
  .pm-card input::placeholder, .pm-card textarea::placeholder { color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-card textarea { resize: vertical; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pm-card input:focus, .pm-card textarea:focus, .pm-slug:focus {
    outline: none; border-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent);
  }
  .pm-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; padding: 0.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius-sm); }
  .pm-tags input { flex: 1; min-width: 6rem; border: 0 !important; padding: 0.25rem 0.35rem !important; background: transparent !important; box-shadow: none !important; }
  .pm-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.85em; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent); }
  .pm-chip button { border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; padding: 0; }
  .pm-permalink { margin: 0.1rem 0 1.1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-slug { color: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 0.15rem; outline: none; }
  .pm-toggle { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); cursor: pointer; }
  .pm-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.85rem; }
  .pm-btn { padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--admin-radius-sm); background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
  .pm-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; }
  .pm-btn-primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
  #pm-signin .pm-btn-primary { width: 100%; }
  #pm-form .pm-btn-primary { padding-inline: 1.6rem; }
  .pm-or { margin: 0.9rem 0; text-align: center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-magic { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .pm-magic input { flex: 1; }
  /* Publish/update status: a live accent ring while the work is in flight (the
     Publish button is disabled), then a settled result line — reads as motion, not
     a static grey label. */
  .pm-status { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--fg); font-family: var(--font-sans); line-height: 1.4; transition: color 0.2s ease; }
  .pm-status:empty { display: none; }
  .pm-status a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .pm-progress {
    display: none; width: 15px; height: 15px; flex: none; border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 28%, transparent);
    border-top-color: var(--accent); animation: pm-spin 0.7s linear infinite;
  }
  .pm-actions:has(#pm-publish:disabled) .pm-progress { display: inline-block; }
  @keyframes pm-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
</style>

<!-- Global (unscoped) styles: the code-block preview DOM is created by Milkdown at
     runtime, so Astro's scoped styles never reach it — target these classes globally. -->
<style is:global>
  .d2-preview { display: flex; justify-content: center; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  .d2-preview svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .d2-error {
    padding: 1rem; color: #e5484d; white-space: pre-wrap;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .plotly-cell { margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: hidden; }
  .plotly-holder { width: 100%; height: 380px; }
  .py-running { padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem; opacity: 0.6; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .py-output {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0.6rem; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--code-bg); color: var(--code-fg); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .plotly-error {
    padding: 0.75rem; margin: 0; color: #e5484d; white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.85em;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .plotly-controls {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .plotly-controls .pc-label { font-weight: 600; opacity: 0.85; }
  .plotly-controls label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.25rem; opacity: 0.85; }
  .plotly-controls input {
    width: 3.5rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px; background: var(--bg); color: inherit;
  }
  /* !important: the Milkdown/Crepe editor theme otherwise overrides editor buttons
     to a transparent background, making this one invisible (white text on white). */
  .plotly-controls button {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem !important; border: 0 !important; border-radius: 6px !important;
    background: var(--accent) !important; color: var(--on-accent) !important; opacity: 1 !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important; font-size: 0.85em !important; cursor: pointer !important;
  }
  .plotly-controls button:disabled { opacity: 0.55 !important; cursor: default !important; }
  .plotly-controls .pc-status { opacity: 0.75; }

  /* ---- Blend the Crepe/Milkdown editor with the site theme (both light + dark) ----
     The Nord theme ships its own palette; remap its CSS variables to the editorial
     tokens so the writing surface matches the published look instead of reading as a
     bright/white sheet. Scoped under #editor-wrap so it out-specifies Nord's .milkdown.
     The admin shell now honours data-theme, so these flip with the toggle. */
  #editor-wrap .milkdown {
    --crepe-color-background: var(--bg);
    --crepe-color-on-background: var(--fg);
    --crepe-color-surface: var(--bg);
    --crepe-color-surface-low: var(--surface);
    --crepe-color-on-surface: var(--fg);
    --crepe-color-on-surface-variant: var(--muted);
    --crepe-color-outline: var(--border);
    --crepe-color-primary: var(--accent);
    --crepe-color-secondary: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent);
    --crepe-color-on-secondary: var(--fg);
    --crepe-color-inverse: var(--fg);
    --crepe-color-on-inverse: var(--bg);
    --crepe-color-inline-code: var(--accent);
    --crepe-color-inline-area: var(--surface);
    --crepe-color-error: #e5484d;
    --crepe-color-hover: var(--admin-hover);
    --crepe-color-selected: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 14%, transparent);
    --crepe-font-title: var(--serif-display);
    --crepe-font-default: var(--serif-body);
    --crepe-font-code: var(--font-mono);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  /* Make the text cursor clearly visible in BOTH themes (Crepe left it unset, so it
     was easy to lose against the paper). A slightly bolder accent caret reads well on
     plum (light) and bronze (dark). */
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror,
  #editor-wrap .milkdown [contenteditable="true"] { caret-color: var(--accent); }
  /* The editor's inline code chip: match the reader's editorial inline code. */
  #editor-wrap .milkdown code:not(pre code) {
    background: var(--paper-2); border: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
  }
  /* Prose rhythm parity with the reader's `.post-body` (global.css) so the WYSIWYG
     surface reads like what publishes — same body size/leading, heading scale,
     paragraph rhythm, blockquote, rule and lists. Typography only: code blocks
     (live CodeMirror), D2 and Plotly widgets stay the editor's own live versions,
     which can't be byte-identical to the static reader render. High-specificity
     (#editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror …) so it out-ranks Crepe's Nord defaults. */
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror { font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink); }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror p { margin: 0 0 1.35em; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror h1 { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 46px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.4em; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror h2 { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(25px, 3.2vw, 34px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 2em 0 0.6em; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror h3 { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 22px; margin: 1.8em 0 0.5em; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror blockquote { margin: 1.8em 0; padding: 6px 0 6px 26px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror blockquote p { font-family: var(--serif-display); font-style: italic; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink); margin: 0; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror hr { border: 0; height: 1px; background: var(--rule); margin: 2.4em 0; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror ul, #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror ol { padding-left: 1.4em; margin: 0 0 1.35em; }
  #editor-wrap .milkdown .ProseMirror li { margin: 0.4em 0; }
</style>

<script>
  import { supabase } from '../../lib/supabase';
  // The dashboard shell (AdminLayout) gates the whole /admin area; boot the editor
  // once an admin is confirmed (or immediately for a returning, cached admin).
  import { whenAdmin, cachedAdmin } from '../../lib/admin-gate';
  import { Crepe } from '@milkdown/crepe';
  import { languages } from '@codemirror/language-data';
  import { LanguageDescription, LanguageSupport, StreamLanguage } from '@codemirror/language';
  import { closeBrackets, closeBracketsKeymap } from '@codemirror/autocomplete';
  import { keymap } from '@codemirror/view';
  import { $prose } from '@milkdown/kit/utils';
  import { Plugin, PluginKey, TextSelection } from '@milkdown/kit/prose/state';
  import { Decoration, DecorationSet } from '@milkdown/kit/prose/view';
  import { renderPlotlyFigure, loadPlotlyJs, makeRotatingGif } from '../../lib/plotly';
  import { mountSeriesPicker } from '../../lib/series-picker';
  // NOTE: the render-at-publish modules (render-post-browser → @astrojs/markdown-remark
  // + Shiki + browser-D2, and assemble-post) are heavy and only needed at publish, so
  // they are DYNAMICALLY imported in the publish handler — not here — to keep the
  // editor's initial bundle light and make the page interactive fast.
  import '@milkdown/crepe/theme/common/style.css';
  import '@milkdown/crepe/theme/nord.css';

  // Register "d2" as a recognized code-block language. Crepe's CodeMirror feature only
  // turns a ```lang fence into a code block for languages it knows (from
  // @codemirror/language-data); "d2" isn't there, so typing ```d2 previously stayed as
  // plain text (while ```ts worked). No grammar is needed — d2 blocks render to a
  // diagram via the D2 preview, not as highlighted source — so this is a minimal
  // no-op language whose only job is to make the fence recognized.
  const d2Language = LanguageDescription.of({
    name: 'd2',
    alias: ['d2'],
    load: () => Promise.resolve(new LanguageSupport(StreamLanguage.define({ token: (s) => { s.next(); return null; } }))),
  });

  // Auto-pair brackets AND quotes across the whole editor (blog-wide, prose side).
  // Typing an opener inserts its closer with the cursor between (e.g. '(|)'); typing
  // a closer/quote that's already next "types over" it; Backspace on an empty pair
  // deletes both. Code blocks get the same behavior via CodeMirror's closeBrackets.
  // NOTE: backtick is deliberately NOT paired here — it collides with Markdown's own
  // inline-code and fenced-code-block (```) shortcuts, which Milkdown handles natively.
  const PAIRS = { '(': ')', '[': ']', '{': '}', '"': '"', "'": "'" };
  const CLOSERS = new Set([')', ']', '}']);
  const QUOTES = new Set(['"', "'"]);

  const bracketPairing = $prose(() => new Plugin({
    props: {
      handleTextInput(view, from, to, text) {
        const { state } = view;
        const closing = PAIRS[text];
        if (closing) {
          if (QUOTES.has(text) && from === to) {
            // Type over an existing identical quote instead of nesting a new pair.
            if (state.doc.textBetween(from, from + 1) === text) {
              view.dispatch(state.tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(state.doc, from + 1)));
              return true;
            }
            // Don't auto-pair a quote right after a word char (contractions: don't, it's).
            const before = from > 0 ? state.doc.textBetween(from - 1, from) : '';
            if (/\w/.test(before)) return false;
          }
          const tr = state.tr;
          if (from !== to) {
            // Wrap the current selection in the pair, keeping it selected.
            const inner = state.doc.textBetween(from, to);
            tr.insertText(text + inner + closing, from, to);
            tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(tr.doc, from + 1, from + 1 + inner.length));
          } else {
            tr.insertText(text + closing, from, to);
            tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(tr.doc, from + 1));
          }
          view.dispatch(tr);
          return true;
        }
        // Type over a bracket closer that's already the next character.
        if (CLOSERS.has(text) && from === to && state.doc.textBetween(from, from + 1) === text) {
          view.dispatch(state.tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(state.doc, from + 1)));
          return true;
        }
        return false;
      },
      handleKeyDown(view, event) {
        if (event.key !== 'Backspace') return false;
        const { state } = view;
        const sel = state.selection;
        if (!sel.empty || sel.from === 0) return false;
        const before = state.doc.textBetween(sel.from - 1, sel.from);
        const after = state.doc.textBetween(sel.from, sel.from + 1);
        // Cursor sits between an empty pair -> delete both sides.
        if (PAIRS[before] && PAIRS[before] === after) {
          view.dispatch(state.tr.delete(sel.from - 1, sel.from + 1));
          return true;
        }
        return false;
      },
    },
  }));

  // Typed-fence → code block. Milkdown's built-in rule converts ```ts but SKIPS
  // languages its letter-only matcher rejects (notably ```d2 — the digit trips it),
  // leaving them as plain text. This catches that: on Enter, if the current paragraph
  // is exactly a ```<lang> fence, replace it with an empty code block of that language.
  // Languages the built-in rule already handles convert BEFORE Enter (so the paragraph
  // is no longer a fence by the time this runs), so the two don't collide.
  const FENCE_RE = /^```([A-Za-z0-9_+#.-]+)$/;
  const fenceCodeBlock = $prose(() => new Plugin({
    props: {
      handleKeyDown(view, event) {
        if (event.key !== 'Enter') return false;
        const { state } = view;
        const { $from, empty } = state.selection;
        if (!empty) return false;
        const parent = $from.parent;
        if (parent.type.name !== 'paragraph') return false;
        const m = FENCE_RE.exec(parent.textContent);
        if (!m) return false;
        const codeType = state.schema.nodes.code_block || state.schema.nodes.codeBlock;
        if (!codeType) return false;
        let node;
        try { node = codeType.create({ language: m[1] }); }
        catch { try { node = codeType.create(); } catch { return false; } }
        const start = $from.before();
        const end = $from.after();
        const tr = state.tr.replaceRangeWith(start, end, node);
        tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(tr.doc, start + 1));
        view.dispatch(tr.scrollIntoView());
        return true;
      },
    },
  }));

  // Lazy-load D2 (@terrastruct/d2, WASM) only when a ```d2 diagram is first
  // previewed, then reuse the one instance. Kept out of the initial editor bundle
  // via import(). The published site renders the same fences at build time
  // (plugins/rehype-d2), so editor preview and live output match.
  let d2Promise = null;
  function loadD2() {
    if (!d2Promise) d2Promise = import('@terrastruct/d2').then(({ D2 }) => new D2());
    return d2Promise;
  }
  // The browser D2 is a SINGLE shared WASM instance and cannot compile/render
  // concurrently — two diagrams rendering at once (e.g. a post with multiple ```d2
  // blocks) corrupt each other, and one comes back as a bad object that renders as
  // "[object Object]". Funnel every render through a serial queue so only one runs at
  // a time. Same reason as the plotly renderQueue.
  let d2Queue = Promise.resolve();
  // Memoize rendered SVG by exact source. The code-block preview re-invokes render on
  // every keystroke/cursor move even when the diagram text is unchanged (switching
  // blocks, editing prose elsewhere), and each WASM compile+render is the slow part —
  // an unchanged diagram should never pay it twice. Bounded LRU-ish (drop oldest) so a
  // long editing session can't grow the cache without limit.
  const d2Cache = new Map();
  const D2_CACHE_MAX = 64;

  // Figures produced by ```python plot cells during this session, keyed by the
  // cell's (trimmed) source. At publish we embed each one as a ```plotly fence so
  // the reader page renders the plot interactively (rehype-plotly + PlotlyReader);
  // Pyodide never runs for readers. Cells that produce no figure aren't cached.
  const plotlyFigureCache = new Map();
  // Non-plot ```python cells that printed something: their captured stdout, keyed by
  // source, so publish can embed it as a notebook-style output block for readers.
  const pyOutputCache = new Map();
  const escOut = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
  // After every ```python cell, embed its result so the reader sees it (Pyodide never
  // runs for readers): a ```plotly fence for a plotting cell, or a <pre class="py-output">
  // block for a cell that printed text. Cells with neither are left untouched.
  function injectCellOutputs(md) {
    return md.replace(/```(?:python|py)[^\n]*\n([\s\S]*?)\n```/g, (whole, code) => {
      const key = code.trim();
      const fig = plotlyFigureCache.get(key) || plotlyFigureCache.get(code);
      if (fig) {
        let json;
        try { json = JSON.stringify(fig); } catch { return whole; }
        return whole + '\n\n```plotly\n' + json + '\n```';
      }
      const out = pyOutputCache.get(key) || pyOutputCache.get(code);
      if (out) return whole + '\n\n<pre class="py-output">' + escOut(out) + '</pre>';
      return whole;
    });
  }

  // Inverse of injectCellOutputs: remove the publish-injected artifacts (a
  // <pre class="py-output"> block or a ```plotly figure fence) so that loading a
  // published post for editing shows only the SOURCE cells. Milkdown would otherwise
  // render the raw injected HTML/JSON as literal text; the live cells re-run in the
  // editor and injectCellOutputs regenerates fresh output on the next publish.
  function stripCellOutputs(md) {
    return md
      .replace(/\n*<pre class="py-output">[\s\S]*?<\/pre>\n*/g, '\n\n')
      .replace(/\n*```plotly\n[\s\S]*?\n```\n*/g, '\n\n');
  }

  function renderD2(code) {
    if (d2Cache.has(code)) {
      // Refresh recency: re-insert so it's treated as most-recently-used.
      const svg = d2Cache.get(code);
      d2Cache.delete(code);
      d2Cache.set(code, svg);
      return Promise.resolve(svg);
    }
    const run = async () => {
      const d2 = await loadD2();
      const res = await d2.compile(code, { pad: 20, noXMLTag: true, themeID: 1, darkThemeID: 1 });
      const svg = await d2.render(res.diagram, res.renderOptions);
      d2Cache.set(code, svg);
      if (d2Cache.size > D2_CACHE_MAX) d2Cache.delete(d2Cache.keys().next().value);
      return svg;
    };
    const result = d2Queue.then(run, run);
    d2Queue = result.then(() => {}, () => {}); // keep the chain alive past errors
    return result;
  }
  function diagramEl(svg) {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'd2-preview';
    el.innerHTML = svg;
    return el;
  }
  function errorEl(err) {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'd2-error';
    el.textContent = 'D2 error: ' + (err && err.message ? err.message : String(err));
    return el;
  }

  // --- Interactive Python plot cells (Plotly) ---------------------------------
  // Each ```python block gets a live, interactive plot rendered right below it —
  // a notebook-style cell. The author's plotly.py runs client-side via Pyodide
  // (lib/plotly) and plotly.js renders the figure, so 3D plots rotate/zoom right
  // in the editor. The panel is a ProseMirror WIDGET decoration (non-editable,
  // outside Crepe's sanitizer) so interactivity survives. Panels are keyed by the
  // python block's index, so a panel (and its plot) persists while you edit —
  // only its contents re-render, debounced.
  const plotlyKey = new PluginKey('plotly-cells');

  const plotlyCells = $prose(() => {
    const panels = new Map(); // key -> panel DOM
    const timers = new Map(); // panel -> debounce timer id
    let plotlyJs = null;

    function render(panel, code) {
      if (panel.__code === code) return;
      panel.__code = code;
      clearTimeout(timers.get(panel));
      if (!code) { panel.replaceChildren(); panel.__ran = false; return; }
      // Show "Running…" only before a cell's FIRST result; later edits keep the last
      // output visible until the new one is ready (no flicker/spam while typing).
      if (!panel.__ran) {
        const s = document.createElement('div');
        s.className = 'py-running';
        s.textContent = 'Running…';
        panel.replaceChildren(s);
      }
      timers.set(panel, setTimeout(async () => {
        let res;
        try {
          res = await renderPlotlyFigure(code);
        } catch (e) {
          res = { error: 'Could not run: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : String(e)) };
        }
        if (panel.__code !== code) return; // superseded by a newer edit
        panel.__ran = true;
        const { figure, stdout, error } = res;
        if (error) {
          const pre = document.createElement('pre');
          pre.className = 'plotly-error';
          pre.textContent = error;
          panel.replaceChildren(pre);
        } else if (figure) {
          // Plotting cell -> interactive plot.
          if (!plotlyJs) plotlyJs = await loadPlotlyJs();
          let holder = panel.querySelector('.plotly-holder');
          if (!holder) {
            holder = document.createElement('div');
            holder.className = 'plotly-holder';
            panel.replaceChildren(holder);
          }
          // Fit the plot to the editor column: drop any hard-coded width/height the
          // figure set (e.g. width=800) so it can't overflow; autosize to the holder.
          const layout = { ...(figure.layout || {}) };
          delete layout.width;
          delete layout.height;
          layout.autosize = true;
          await plotlyJs.react(holder, figure.data || [], layout, { responsive: true, displaylogo: false });
          requestAnimationFrame(() => { try { plotlyJs.Plots.resize(holder); } catch {} });
          updateControls(panel, holder, figure);
          // Remember this cell's figure so publish can embed it for readers.
          plotlyFigureCache.set(code, figure);
        } else {
          // Non-plotting cell -> a notebook-style output block showing stdout. If the
          // cell printed nothing, show nothing (no clutter). Cache the text so publish
          // can embed it for readers (see injectCellOutputs).
          const out = (stdout || '').replace(/\s+$/, '');
          if (out) {
            pyOutputCache.set(code, out);
            const pre = document.createElement('pre');
            pre.className = 'py-output';
            pre.textContent = out;
            panel.replaceChildren(pre);
          } else {
            pyOutputCache.delete(code);
            panel.replaceChildren();
          }
        }
      }, 700));
    }

    // For 3D figures, offer a rotating-GIF export below the plot (author sets the
    // frame count and fps). 2D figures get no controls.
    function updateControls(panel, holder, figure) {
      const types = (figure.data || []).map((t) => t && t.type).filter(Boolean);
      const is3d = !!(figure.layout && figure.layout.scene) ||
        types.some((t) => /3d$/.test(t) || ['surface', 'mesh3d', 'cone', 'streamtube', 'volume', 'isosurface'].includes(t));
      let bar = panel.querySelector('.plotly-controls');
      if (!is3d) { if (bar) bar.remove(); return; }
      if (bar) return; // already present
      bar = document.createElement('div');
      bar.className = 'plotly-controls';
      bar.innerHTML =
        '<span class="pc-label">Rotating GIF</span>' +
        '<label>frames <input type="number" class="pc-frames" value="36" min="4" max="180"></label>' +
        '<label>fps <input type="number" class="pc-fps" value="15" min="1" max="60"></label>' +
        '<button type="button" class="pc-gif">Download GIF</button>' +
        '<span class="pc-status"></span>';
      const btn = bar.querySelector('.pc-gif');
      const status = bar.querySelector('.pc-status');
      btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const frames = Math.max(4, Math.min(180, parseInt(bar.querySelector('.pc-frames').value, 10) || 36));
        const fps = Math.max(1, Math.min(60, parseInt(bar.querySelector('.pc-fps').value, 10) || 15));
        btn.disabled = true;
        status.textContent = 'Rendering… 0%';
        try {
          const blob = await makeRotatingGif(holder, {
            frames, fps,
            onProgress: (p) => { status.textContent = 'Rendering… ' + Math.round(p * 100) + '%'; },
          });
          const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
          const a = document.createElement('a');
          a.href = url;
          a.download = 'plot.gif';
          document.body.appendChild(a);
          a.click();
          a.remove();
          URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
          status.textContent = 'Saved · ' + Math.round(blob.size / 1024) + ' KB';
        } catch (e) {
          status.textContent = 'Failed: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : String(e));
        } finally {
          btn.disabled = false;
        }
      });
      panel.appendChild(bar);
    }

    function build(state) {
      const decos = [];
      const used = new Set();
      let i = 0;
      state.doc.descendants((node, pos) => {
        if (node.type.name !== 'code_block') return;
        const lang = (node.attrs.language || '').toLowerCase();
        if (lang !== 'python' && lang !== 'py') return;
        const key = 'py-' + i++;
        used.add(key);
        let panel = panels.get(key);
        if (!panel) {
          panel = document.createElement('div');
          panel.className = 'plotly-cell';
          panels.set(key, panel);
        }
        render(panel, node.textContent.trim());
        decos.push(Decoration.widget(pos + node.nodeSize, panel, {
          key, side: 1, ignoreSelection: true, stopEvent: () => true,
        }));
      });
      // Drop panels whose block was removed.
      for (const [k, p] of panels) {
        if (!used.has(k)) {
          clearTimeout(timers.get(p));
          timers.delete(p);
          if (plotlyJs) { try { plotlyJs.purge(p.querySelector('.plotly-holder')); } catch {} }
          panels.delete(k);
        }
      }
      return DecorationSet.create(state.doc, decos);
    }

    return new Plugin({
      key: plotlyKey,
      state: {
        init: (_, state) => build(state),
        apply: (tr, old, _o, newState) => (tr.docChanged ? build(newState) : old),
      },
      props: { decorations(state) { return plotlyKey.getState(state); } },
    });
  });

  const wrap = document.getElementById('editor-wrap');
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('editor-status');

  async function init() {
    // Access is handled by the dashboard shell (AdminLayout): it reveals /admin only
    // for a confirmed admin, and every publish/edit is re-verified server-side
    // (functions/api/publish.js + /api/admin/*). init() runs only after boot() below.
    wrap.hidden = false;

    // New post → restore the local autosaved draft. Editing an existing post
    // (/admin/write?slug=<slug>) → load its Markdown from the content collection.
    const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    const editSlug = params.get('slug');
    const DRAFT_KEY = 'aysr:editor-draft';                          // legacy single-slot key (fallback)
    const draftKeyFor = (id: string) => 'aysr:editor-draft:' + id; // per-draft local cache
    const wantNew = params.has('new');
    // The draft slot this session works on: a specific ?draft=<id>, or (below) the
    // most-recent draft, or a freshly-minted id for a brand-new post. Each new post is
    // its own row keyed by this id, so starting a new one never overwrites the last.
    let currentDraftId = params.get('draft') || '';
    // Durable drafts: the signed-in admin's id, used to read/write their single
    // draft row in Supabase (RLS-scoped) so a draft survives a browser clear or a
    // switch of device. Best-effort — null if the session isn't ready.
    let draftUid = null;
    try { const { data: s } = await supabase.auth.getSession(); draftUid = (s && s.session && s.session.user && s.session.user.id) || null; } catch {}

    let startDoc = '# New post\n\nStart writing.\n';
    let restoredMsg = '';
    // When editing, this carries the existing post's identity/metadata into the
    // publish modal so the slug/date/tags are preserved (not re-derived).
    let editing = null;
    // Set if an edit-load was requested but failed — we must NOT silently fall back to
    // a blank new post (which would clobber the local draft and, on publish, create a
    // new file instead of updating). Autosave stays off and Publish is disabled.
    let editLoadFailed = false;

    if (editSlug) {
      statusEl.textContent = 'Loading…';
      try {
        // Load the DB post (the ONE store) for re-editing: author_get_post returns the caller's own
        // post's Markdown + metadata. body_md is stored WITHOUT the leading "# Title" H1, so re-add
        // it the way a new post starts (publish strips it back out); strip any injected cell outputs.
        const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('author_get_post', { p_slug: editSlug });
        if (error) throw error;
        const row = Array.isArray(data) ? data[0] : data;
        if (!row) throw new Error('Post not found');
        const bodyOnly = stripCellOutputs(String(row.body_md || ''));
        const title = row.title || editSlug;
        startDoc = `# ${title}\n\n${bodyOnly.replace(/^\n+/, '')}`;
        editing = {
          id: row.id,
          slug: row.slug || editSlug,
          title,
          description: row.description || '',
          tags: Array.isArray(row.tags) ? row.tags.map(String) : [],
          pubDate: row.pub_date ? String(row.pub_date).slice(0, 10) : '',
          draft: row.status === 'draft' || row.status === 'scheduled',
          series: row.series_title || row.series_slug || '',
          seriesOrder: row.series_part != null ? String(row.series_part) : '',
          seriesTotal: row.series_total != null ? String(row.series_total) : '',
          seriesStatus: '',
          seriesPlanned: [],
          gateable: row.gateable === true,
        };
        restoredMsg = 'Editing “' + title + '”';
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('[editor] load-for-edit failed', e);
        editLoadFailed = true;
        statusEl.textContent = 'Couldn’t load that post — refresh to retry.';
      }
    } else if (!wantNew) {
      // Reopen a draft: the requested ?draft=<id>, else the most-recent one. Prefer the
      // durable DB copy (this device may have been cleared, or it was written elsewhere);
      // fall back to the per-device local cache. If none exists we fall through to a fresh
      // blank doc (and a new id is minted below).
      let savedDraft = null;
      try {
        if (draftUid) {
          let q = supabase.from('drafts').select('id, content').eq('user_id', draftUid);
          q = currentDraftId
            ? q.eq('id', currentDraftId).maybeSingle()
            : q.order('updated_at', { ascending: false }).limit(1).maybeSingle();
          const { data: row } = await q;
          if (row && typeof (row as any).content === 'string') { savedDraft = (row as any).content; currentDraftId = (row as any).id; }
        }
      } catch {}
      if (savedDraft == null) {
        try { savedDraft = localStorage.getItem(currentDraftId ? draftKeyFor(currentDraftId) : DRAFT_KEY); } catch {}
      }
      if (savedDraft != null && savedDraft.trim()) { startDoc = savedDraft; restoredMsg = 'Draft restored'; }
    }
    // A brand-new post (or one we couldn't match to an existing row) gets its own id.
    if (!editSlug && !currentDraftId) { try { currentDraftId = crypto.randomUUID(); } catch { currentDraftId = 'd' + Date.now() + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8); } }

    const crepe = new Crepe({
      root: document.getElementById('milkdown'),
      defaultValue: startDoc,
      featureConfigs: {
        // Language-aware code blocks: hand the CodeMirror feature the full
        // language set (from @codemirror/language-data) so a block tagged ts /
        // python / rust / etc. loads that grammar and highlights accordingly,
        // with a language picker in the block. Matches the build-time Shiki output.
        [Crepe.Feature.CodeMirror]: {
          languages: [d2Language, ...languages],
          // Auto-close brackets/quotes: typing '(' inserts '()' with the cursor
          // between (i.e. '(|)'), and Backspace on the empty pair removes BOTH.
          extensions: [closeBrackets(), keymap.of(closeBracketsKeymap)],
          // Live diagrams: for a ```d2 block, render it client-side (D2 WASM) into
          // the block's preview panel (a toggle appears in the block's toolbar).
          // undefined return = async; applyPreview() swaps in the SVG when ready.
          // Any other language returns null -> no preview toggle, no overhead. On
          // publish the same ```d2 fence is rendered at build time by
          // plugins/rehype-d2, so editor preview and live site stay identical.
          renderPreview: (language, content, applyPreview) => {
            const lang = (language || '').toLowerCase();
            const code = content.trim();
            if (!code) return null;
            if (lang === 'd2') {
              renderD2(code)
                .then((svg) => applyPreview(diagramEl(svg)))
                .catch((err) => applyPreview(errorEl(err)));
              return undefined;
            }
            // Python plots are handled by the interactive Plotly panel plugin
            // (rendered below the block), not by this sanitized preview.
            return null;
          },
          previewLabel: 'Diagram',
        },
      },
    });
    let saveTimer = null;
    // Gate the chrome hook: markdownUpdated can fire during crepe.create() — before
    // the chrome block below has initialised its state — so only call updateChrome
    // once that state exists (set true at the end of the chrome block).
    let chromeInit = false;
    crepe.on((api) => {
      api.markdownUpdated((_ctx, md) => {
        // Live chrome (word count, read time, outline, goal, session log) — runs for
        // both new and editing; never touches the doc. updateChrome is hoisted below.
        if (chromeInit) updateChrome(md);
        // Editing a published post doesn't autosave to the local draft slot (that's the
        // new-post scratchpad) — edits are committed on Publish. A failed edit-load must
        // also never write the draft slot. New posts autosave.
        if (editLoadFailed) return;
        if (editing) { statusEl.textContent = 'Unsaved edits — Publish to save'; return; }
        statusEl.textContent = 'Saving…';
        clearTimeout(saveTimer);
        saveTimer = setTimeout(async () => {
          try { if (currentDraftId) localStorage.setItem(draftKeyFor(currentDraftId), md); } catch {}
          // Durable copy — upsert THIS draft's own row (keyed by id, RLS-scoped) with a
          // title for the Drafts list. Best-effort; a failure keeps the local copy.
          try {
            const dTitle = ((md.match(/^#\s+(.+)$/m) || [])[1] || '').trim().slice(0, 140) || 'Untitled draft';
            if (draftUid && currentDraftId) await supabase.from('drafts').upsert({ id: currentDraftId, user_id: draftUid, content: md, title: dTitle, updated_at: new Date().toISOString() }, { onConflict: 'id' });
            statusEl.textContent = 'Saved';
          } catch { statusEl.textContent = 'Saved locally'; }
        }, 800);
      });
    });

    crepe.editor.use(bracketPairing);
    crepe.editor.use(fenceCodeBlock);
    crepe.editor.use(plotlyCells);
    await crepe.create();
    if (restoredMsg) statusEl.textContent = restoredMsg;

    // ======================================================================
    // WRITE CHROME — session stats, outline, notes, length target, focus mode.
    // The Milkdown canvas above is the source of truth; everything here READS its
    // Markdown and drives the top bar / rail / status bar. It never mutates the
    // doc. Notes, target and the session log are private to this device
    // (localStorage), keyed to the post being edited (or the new-post scratch).
    // ======================================================================
    const escHtml = (s) => String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]));
    const wc = {
      words: document.getElementById('w-words'), read: document.getElementById('w-read'),
      today: document.getElementById('w-today'), streak: document.getElementById('w-streak'),
      goalWrap: document.getElementById('w-goalwrap'), goalBar: document.getElementById('w-goalbar'),
      goalText: document.getElementById('w-goaltext'), line: document.getElementById('w-statusline'),
      outline: document.getElementById('r-outline'), written: document.getElementById('r-written'),
    };
    const docKey = editing ? ('post:' + editing.slug) : 'draft';
    const NOTES_KEY = 'aysr:notes:' + docKey;
    const TARGET_KEY = 'aysr:target:' + docKey;
    const SESS_KEY = 'aysr:write-sessions';
    const dayStr = (d) => d.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
    const today = dayStr(new Date());

    const countWords = (md) => {
      const prose = String(md || '')
        .replace(/```[\s\S]*?```/g, ' ').replace(/`[^`]*`/g, ' ')
        .replace(/^#{1,6}\s+/gm, '').replace(/[*_>#\[\]()!]+/g, ' ');
      const m = prose.trim().match(/\S+/g); return m ? m.length : 0;
    };
    const readMin = (w) => Math.max(1, Math.round(w / 200));
    let target = 0;
    try { target = parseInt(localStorage.getItem(TARGET_KEY) || '', 10) || 0; } catch {}

    function updateChrome(md) {
      const w = countWords(md), r = readMin(w);
      // Persist the live word count for this doc so the Drafts view can show real
      // progress bars (per-device, alongside the note + target it already reads).
      try { localStorage.setItem('aysr:words:' + docKey, String(w)); } catch {}
      if (wc.words) wc.words.textContent = w.toLocaleString();
      if (wc.read) wc.read.textContent = r + ' min';
      if (wc.written) wc.written.textContent = w.toLocaleString();
      if (wc.line) wc.line.textContent = w.toLocaleString() + ' word' + (w === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' · ' + r + ' min read';
      if (wc.goalWrap) {
        if (target > 0) {
          wc.goalWrap.hidden = false;
          wc.goalBar.style.width = Math.min(100, Math.round((w / target) * 100)) + '%';
          wc.goalText.textContent = w.toLocaleString() + ' of ' + target.toLocaleString();
        } else wc.goalWrap.hidden = true;
      }
      try {
        const sess = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SESS_KEY) || '{}');
        if (!sess[today] || typeof sess[today].start !== 'number') sess[today] = { start: w, last: w };
        sess[today].last = w;
        localStorage.setItem(SESS_KEY, JSON.stringify(sess));
        if (wc.today) wc.today.textContent = Math.max(0, sess[today].last - sess[today].start).toLocaleString();
        let streak = 0; const d = new Date(today + 'T00:00:00');
        while (sess[dayStr(d)]) { streak++; d.setDate(d.getDate() - 1); }
        if (wc.streak) { wc.streak.hidden = streak < 2; wc.streak.textContent = streak + '-day streak'; }
      } catch {}
      renderOutline(md);
    }

    function renderOutline(md) {
      const host = wc.outline; if (!host) return;
      const lines = String(md || '').split('\n');
      const items = []; let cur = null; let inFence = false;
      const flush = () => { if (cur) { cur.words = countWords(cur.buf.join('\n')); items.push(cur); } };
      for (const ln of lines) {
        // Track fenced code (``` / ~~~) so a code/D2 comment line ("# …") is NEVER
        // mistaken for a Markdown heading — only real prose headings become outline items.
        if (/^\s{0,3}(```|~~~)/.test(ln)) { inFence = !inFence; if (cur) cur.buf.push(ln); continue; }
        if (inFence) { if (cur) cur.buf.push(ln); continue; }
        const h = ln.match(/^(#{1,6})\s+(.+)$/);
        if (h) { flush(); cur = { level: h[1].length, text: h[2].trim(), buf: [] }; }
        else if (cur) cur.buf.push(ln);
      }
      flush();
      if (!items.length) { host.innerHTML = '<li class="rempty">Headings appear here as you write.</li>'; return; }
      host.innerHTML = items.map((it, i) => {
        const isTitle = i === 0 && it.level === 1;
        const cls = it.level >= 2 ? ' class="sub"' : '';
        const tally = isTitle ? 'title' : (it.words ? it.words.toLocaleString() : '·');
        return '<li' + cls + ' data-i="' + i + '"><span>' + escHtml(it.text) + '</span><span class="w">' + tally + '</span></li>';
      }).join('');
    }

    // Rail tabs
    const rtabs = document.getElementById('rtabs');
    if (rtabs) rtabs.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = e.target.closest('button[data-p]'); if (!b) return;
      rtabs.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b));
      wrap.querySelectorAll('.rpane').forEach((p) => p.classList.toggle('on', p.dataset.pane === b.dataset.p));
    });
    // Outline → scroll to the matching heading in the live editor
    if (wc.outline) wc.outline.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const li = e.target.closest('li[data-i]'); if (!li) return;
      const hs = document.querySelectorAll('#milkdown h1, #milkdown h2, #milkdown h3, #milkdown h4, #milkdown h5, #milkdown h6');
      const el = hs[parseInt(li.dataset.i, 10)];
      if (el) el.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    });
    // Notes — private, per-post, this device
    const notesHost = document.getElementById('r-notes');
    const noteInput = document.getElementById('r-note-input');
    const loadNotes = () => { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(NOTES_KEY) || '[]'); } catch { return []; } };
    function renderNotes() {
      const list = loadNotes();
      notesHost.innerHTML = list.length
        ? list.slice().reverse().map((n) => '<li><span class="w">' + escHtml(n.when || '') + '</span>' + escHtml(n.text) + '</li>').join('')
        : '<li class="rempty">No notes yet. These stay private — never published.</li>';
    }
    if (noteInput) noteInput.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key !== 'Enter') return; e.preventDefault();
      const t = noteInput.value.trim(); if (!t) return;
      const list = loadNotes();
      list.push({ text: t, when: new Date().toLocaleDateString(undefined, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' }) });
      try { localStorage.setItem(NOTES_KEY, JSON.stringify(list)); } catch {}
      noteInput.value = ''; renderNotes();
    });
    renderNotes();
    // Length target
    const targetInput = document.getElementById('r-target');
    if (targetInput) {
      if (target > 0) targetInput.value = String(target);
      targetInput.addEventListener('input', () => {
        target = parseInt(targetInput.value, 10) || 0;
        try { target > 0 ? localStorage.setItem(TARGET_KEY, String(target)) : localStorage.removeItem(TARGET_KEY); } catch {}
        try { updateChrome(crepe.getMarkdown()); } catch {}
      });
    }
    // Post-tab identity + top-bar state
    const wState = document.getElementById('w-state');
    const rSeries = document.getElementById('r-series');
    const rState2 = document.getElementById('r-state2');
    if (editing) {
      if (rSeries) rSeries.textContent = editing.series || 'None';
      const label = editing.draft ? 'Draft' : 'Published';
      if (rState2) rState2.textContent = label;
      if (wState) { wState.textContent = editing.draft ? 'Draft' : 'Editing'; if (!editing.draft) wState.classList.add('live'); }
    }
    // "Saved" mirrors the autosave status text
    const rSaved = document.getElementById('r-saved');
    if (rSaved) {
      const sync = () => { rSaved.textContent = statusEl.textContent || '—'; };
      try { new MutationObserver(sync).observe(statusEl, { childList: true, characterData: true, subtree: true }); } catch {}
      sync();
    }
    // Focus mode: shed the studio navigation (sidebar + topbar, via a body-level
    // class the layout CSS keys off) but keep the writing instruments — the
    // progress bar and the Outline/Notes/Post rail. ⌘\ toggles, Esc exits, and
    // the Focus button (in the now-visible .wtop) or the on-screen hint also return.
    const focusBtn = document.getElementById('focusbtn');
    const setFocus = (on) => {
      const state = on == null ? !wrap.classList.contains('focus') : on;
      wrap.classList.toggle('focus', state);
      document.body.classList.toggle('studio-focus', state);
    };
    if (focusBtn) focusBtn.addEventListener('click', () => setFocus());
    const openPub = document.getElementById('r-openpub');
    if (openPub) openPub.addEventListener('click', () => document.getElementById('publish-btn').click());
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Escape' && wrap.classList.contains('focus')) { setFocus(false); return; }
      if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === '\\') { e.preventDefault(); setFocus(); }
      if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === 'Enter') { e.preventDefault(); document.getElementById('publish-btn').click(); }
    });
    // Chrome state is ready — allow the live hook to run, then paint once.
    chromeInit = true;
    try { updateChrome(crepe.getMarkdown()); } catch {}
    // A failed edit-load must not let the author publish (that would create a new post
    // and orphan the one they meant to edit). Block publishing until they refresh.
    if (editLoadFailed) {
      const pb = document.getElementById('publish-btn');
      if (pb) pb.disabled = true;
    }

    // WARM-UP: now that the editor is interactive, prefetch the heavy bits during idle
    // time — the browser's spare cycles while you read/type/navigate — so nothing is
    // paid on the critical load path yet everything is ready by the time you need it:
    //   • the render-at-publish pipeline (markdown-remark + Shiki + browser-D2 assembler)
    //     — import() caches the module, so the publish handler's import() is then instant.
    //   • the D2 WASM instance — so the first ```d2 preview renders without cold-start lag.
    // requestIdleCallback runs only when the main thread is free (never competing with
    // typing); a timeout fallback covers browsers without it. All best-effort — a failed
    // prefetch just means that path pays its own load later, exactly as before.
    const warmUp = () => {
      import('../../lib/render-post-browser.mjs').catch(() => {});
      import('../../lib/assemble-post.mjs').catch(() => {});
      loadD2().catch(() => {});
    };
    if (typeof requestIdleCallback === 'function') requestIdleCallback(warmUp, { timeout: 4000 });
    else setTimeout(warmUp, 1500);

    // "New" starts a fresh post in its OWN draft slot. It is non-destructive now:
    // the current draft is already saved as its own row, so nothing is lost — ?new
    // mints a brand-new id on load. No confirm needed (it can't nuke your work).
    const newBtn = document.getElementById('new-draft');
    newBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { location.href = '/admin/write?new=1'; });

    // "Preview" renders the current draft through the REAL publish pipeline (Shiki,
    // KaTeX, D2, live cell outputs) and opens the finished post in a new tab — exactly
    // the HTML readers get. The window is opened synchronously (before any await) so the
    // browser doesn't block it as a popup.
    document.getElementById('get-md').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const btn = document.getElementById('get-md');
      const w = window.open('', '_blank');
      try { if (w) { w.document.write('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Preview…</title><body style="margin:0;font:15px system-ui;color:#8a8a8a;display:grid;place-items:center;height:100vh">Rendering preview…</body>'); w.document.close(); } } catch {}
      const label = btn.textContent; btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Rendering…';
      try {
        const md = crepe.getMarkdown();
        const title = ((md.match(/^#\s+(.+)$/m) || [])[1] || 'Untitled').trim();
        const body = injectCellOutputs(md.replace(/^#\s+.+\n+/, ''));
        const description = (document.getElementById('pm-post-desc') as HTMLTextAreaElement | null)?.value?.trim() || '';
        const [{ renderPostBodyBrowser }, { assemblePostHtml }] = await Promise.all([
          import('../../lib/render-post-browser.mjs'),
          import('../../lib/assemble-post.mjs'),
        ]);
        const bodyHtml = await renderPostBodyBrowser(body);
        const shellHtml = await (await fetch('/post-shell', { cache: 'no-store' })).text();
        const html = assemblePostHtml(shellHtml, {
          slug: (editing && editing.slug) || 'preview', title, description,
          author: 'Preview', pubDate: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10),
          tags: pubTags, bodyMarkdown: body, bodyHtml,
        });
        if (w) { w.document.open(); w.document.write(html); w.document.close(); }
        else { window.open(URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([html], { type: 'text/html' })), '_blank'); }
      } catch (e: any) {
        const msg = 'Preview failed: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : e);
        if (w && w.document && w.document.body) w.document.body.textContent = msg; else alert(msg);
      } finally { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = label; }
    });

    // --- Publish (premium modal) --------------------------------------------
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const modal = $('publish-modal');
    const slugify = (s) => s.toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').slice(0, 80);
    const firstHeading = (md) => { const m = md.match(/^#\s+(.+)$/m); return m ? m[1].trim() : ''; };
    const yaml = (v) => JSON.stringify(String(v == null ? '' : v)); // JSON-style scalar is valid YAML
    // Seed from the post being edited so its tags show as chips; empty for a new post.
    let pubTags = editing && Array.isArray(editing.tags) ? editing.tags.slice(0, 5) : [];
    let slugEdited = false;

    const openModal = () => {
      modal.hidden = false;
      // Show the sign-in view immediately so the card is never blank while the async
      // session check runs; refreshAuthView() swaps to the form if already signed in.
      $('pm-signin').hidden = false;
      $('pm-form').hidden = true;
      // Reset the "when" picker to Publish-now on every open.
      whenChoice = 'now';
      document.getElementById('schedbox')?.classList.add('off');
      document.querySelectorAll('#whenpick .pk').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('on', (x as HTMLElement).dataset.w === 'now'));
      refreshAuthView();
    };
    const closeModal = () => { modal.hidden = true; };
    $('publish-btn').addEventListener('click', openModal);
    $('pm-close').addEventListener('click', closeModal);
    modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if (e.target === modal) closeModal(); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Escape' && !modal.hidden) closeModal(); });

    // --- Press-check footer + pre-flight checklist ----------------------------
    // The publish ENGINE (#pm-publish's handler) is unchanged. #pm-draft is a hidden
    // flag the footer sets on pointer-down (before the handler's click reads it):
    // Save-draft = on; the primary button = on when SCHEDULING (a scheduled post is a
    // hidden draft with a publishAt), off for Publish now. Everything the checklist
    // shows is real editor/post state — no mock numbers.
    $('pm-cancel').addEventListener('click', closeModal);
    $('pm-publish').addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { $('pm-draft').checked = whenChoice === 'later'; });
    $('pm-save-draft').addEventListener('click', () => { $('pm-draft').checked = true; whenChoice = 'now'; $('pm-publish').click(); });

    // "Who can read it" — Free / Paid. The publish handler reads `accessChoice` (writes
    // frontmatter `gateable`), and applies the suggested price to post_paywall once the
    // post is live. Members-only + scheduling aren't in our backend (disabled in markup).
    let accessChoice = 'free';
    const accpick = $('accpick');
    accpick.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button[data-a]') as HTMLElement | null; if (!b) return;
      accessChoice = b.dataset.a!;
      accpick.querySelectorAll('.pk').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b));
      $('pricebox').classList.toggle('off', accessChoice !== 'paid');
      refreshSheet();
    });

    // "When" — Publish now vs Schedule it. Scheduling saves the post as a HIDDEN draft
    // with a `publishAt`; the cron (.github/workflows/scheduled-publish.yml) flips it
    // live at that time. The primary button relabels to "Schedule" while scheduling.
    let whenChoice = 'now';
    const whenpick = $('whenpick');
    const schedDate = $('pm-sched-date') as HTMLInputElement; // hidden, value = YYYY-MM-DD
    const schedTime = $('pm-sched-time') as HTMLInputElement; // hidden, value = HH:MM
    const schedTz = $('pm-sched-tz') as HTMLInputElement;     // hidden, value = IANA zone

    // Fully custom date / time / zone pickers. Native <input type=date/time> and <select>
    // render OS popups that can't be themed to the Studio, so we roll our own on-brand
    // popovers; each writes into the hidden input the scheduling code above reads.
    const sched = (() => {
      const now = new Date();
      const offMin = (tz: string) => {
        try {
          const p = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone: tz, hour12: false, year: 'numeric', month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit' }).formatToParts(now);
          const m: any = {}; for (const x of p) m[x.type] = x.value;
          const asUTC = Date.UTC(+m.year, +m.month - 1, +m.day, (+m.hour) % 24, +m.minute, +m.second);
          return Math.round((asUTC - now.getTime()) / 60000);
        } catch { return 0; }
      };
      const fmtOff = (min: number) => `UTC${min < 0 ? '−' : '+'}${String(Math.floor(Math.abs(min) / 60)).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(Math.abs(min) % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`;
      let zones: string[] = [];
      try { const f = (Intl as any).supportedValuesOf; if (f) zones = f('timeZone'); } catch {}
      let here = 'UTC';
      try { here = Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone || 'UTC'; } catch {}
      if (!zones.length) zones = ['UTC', 'America/Los_Angeles', 'America/New_York', 'America/Sao_Paulo', 'Europe/London', 'Europe/Berlin', 'Africa/Johannesburg', 'Asia/Dubai', 'Asia/Kolkata', 'Asia/Singapore', 'Asia/Tokyo', 'Australia/Sydney'];
      if (!zones.includes(here)) zones.unshift(here);
      // People think in "how far ahead/behind me", not zone names — so show ONE recognizable
      // zone per DISTINCT current offset (no duplicates) on a clean 30-minute grid, ordered
      // by offset. The author's own zone always represents its own offset.
      const hereOff = offMin(here);
      const byOff = new Map<number, string[]>();
      for (const z of zones) { const o = offMin(z); const a = byOff.get(o); if (a) a.push(z); else byOff.set(o, [z]); }
      const PREF = ['Pacific/Midway', 'Pacific/Honolulu', 'America/Anchorage', 'America/Los_Angeles', 'America/Denver', 'America/Chicago', 'America/New_York', 'America/Halifax', 'America/Sao_Paulo', 'Atlantic/Azores', 'UTC', 'Europe/London', 'Europe/Paris', 'Europe/Athens', 'Europe/Moscow', 'Asia/Tehran', 'Asia/Dubai', 'Asia/Kabul', 'Asia/Karachi', 'Asia/Kolkata', 'Asia/Yangon', 'Asia/Dhaka', 'Asia/Bangkok', 'Asia/Shanghai', 'Asia/Tokyo', 'Australia/Adelaide', 'Australia/Sydney', 'Pacific/Noumea', 'Pacific/Auckland', 'Pacific/Kiritimati'];
      const repFor = (off: number) => { if (off === hereOff) return here; const g = byOff.get(off) || []; for (const p of PREF) if (g.indexOf(p) >= 0) return p; return g[0]; };
      const offsets = Array.from(byOff.keys()).filter((o) => o % 30 === 0);
      if (offsets.indexOf(hereOff) < 0) offsets.push(hereOff);
      offsets.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const TZ = offsets.map((off) => { const z = repFor(off); return { z, off, label: `(${fmtOff(off)}) ${z.replace(/_/g, ' ')}` }; });
      schedTz.value = here;

      const esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' } as any)[c]);
      const centerIn = (c: HTMLElement | null, el: HTMLElement | null) => { if (!c || !el) return; const cr = c.getBoundingClientRect(), er = el.getBoundingClientRect(); c.scrollTop += (er.top - cr.top) - (c.clientHeight / 2 - er.height / 2); };

      // one popover open at a time; outside-click / Esc closes.
      let open: { wrap: HTMLElement; trigger: HTMLElement; panel: HTMLElement } | null = null;
      const closeAll = () => { if (open) { open.panel.hidden = true; open.trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'); open = null; } };
      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if (open && !open.wrap.contains(e.target as Node)) closeAll(); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Escape' && open) { closeAll(); } });
      const wire = (id: string, build: (panel: HTMLElement) => void) => {
        const wrap = $(id); const trigger = wrap.querySelector('.spick') as HTMLElement; const panel = wrap.querySelector('.spop') as HTMLElement;
        trigger.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
          e.stopPropagation();
          const wasOpen = !!open && open.panel === panel; closeAll();
          if (!wasOpen) { build(panel); panel.hidden = false; trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true'); open = { wrap, trigger, panel }; (panel.querySelector('[data-focus]') as HTMLElement | null)?.focus(); }
        });
      };

      const dateLabel = $('sp-date-v'), timeLabel = $('sp-time-v'), tzLabel = $('sp-tz-v');
      const niceDate = (v: string) => { if (!v) return 'Pick a date'; const [Y, M, D] = v.split('-').map(Number); return new Date(Date.UTC(Y, M - 1, D)).toLocaleDateString(undefined, { weekday: 'short', month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' }); };
      const renderLabels = () => {
        dateLabel.textContent = niceDate(schedDate.value);
        timeLabel.textContent = schedTime.value || 'Set time';
        const f = TZ.find((t) => t.z === schedTz.value); tzLabel.textContent = f ? f.label : (schedTz.value || 'Time zone');
      };

      // ---- calendar ----
      let viewY: number, viewM: number;
      const drawCal = (panel: HTMLElement) => {
        const first = new Date(viewY, viewM, 1); const start = first.getDay(); const days = new Date(viewY, viewM + 1, 0).getDate();
        const monthName = first.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
        const cur = schedDate.value; const t = new Date(); const tY = t.getFullYear(), tM = t.getMonth(), tD = t.getDate();
        let cells = '';
        for (let i = 0; i < start; i++) cells += '<span class="cal-x"></span>';
        for (let d = 1; d <= days; d++) {
          const iso = `${viewY}-${String(viewM + 1).padStart(2, '0')}-${String(d).padStart(2, '0')}`;
          cells += `<button type="button" class="cal-d${cur === iso ? ' sel' : ''}${viewY === tY && viewM === tM && d === tD ? ' today' : ''}" data-iso="${iso}">${d}</button>`;
        }
        panel.innerHTML = `<div class="cal-h"><button type="button" class="cal-nav" data-mv="-1" aria-label="Previous month">‹</button><b>${monthName}</b><button type="button" class="cal-nav" data-mv="1" aria-label="Next month">›</button></div><div class="cal-wd"><span>Su</span><span>Mo</span><span>Tu</span><span>We</span><span>Th</span><span>Fr</span><span>Sa</span></div><div class="cal-g">${cells}</div><div class="cal-f"><button type="button" data-cal="clear">Clear</button><button type="button" data-cal="today">Today</button></div>`;
        panel.querySelectorAll('[data-mv]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); viewM += Number((b as HTMLElement).dataset.mv); if (viewM < 0) { viewM = 11; viewY--; } if (viewM > 11) { viewM = 0; viewY++; } drawCal(panel); }));
        panel.querySelectorAll('.cal-d').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); schedDate.value = (b as HTMLElement).dataset.iso!; renderLabels(); closeAll(); }));
        panel.querySelector('[data-cal="clear"]')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); schedDate.value = ''; renderLabels(); closeAll(); });
        panel.querySelector('[data-cal="today"]')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); const n = new Date(); viewY = n.getFullYear(); viewM = n.getMonth(); schedDate.value = `${viewY}-${String(viewM + 1).padStart(2, '0')}-${String(n.getDate()).padStart(2, '0')}`; renderLabels(); closeAll(); });
      };
      const buildDate = (panel: HTMLElement) => {
        const cur = schedDate.value ? schedDate.value.split('-').map(Number) : null;
        const base = cur ? new Date(cur[0], cur[1] - 1, cur[2]) : new Date();
        viewY = base.getFullYear(); viewM = base.getMonth();
        drawCal(panel);
      };

      // ---- time (hour + minute columns) ----
      const buildTime = (panel: HTMLElement) => {
        const [ch, cm] = (schedTime.value || '').split(':');
        const col = (n: number, sel: string, kind: string) => { let h = ''; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const v = String(i).padStart(2, '0'); h += `<button type="button" class="tm-i${v === sel ? ' sel' : ''}" data-kind="${kind}" data-v="${v}">${v}</button>`; } return h; };
        panel.innerHTML = `<div class="tm-cols"><div class="tm-col" data-col="h">${col(24, ch, 'h')}</div><div class="tm-col" data-col="m">${col(60, cm, 'm')}</div></div>`;
        const setPart = (kind: string, v: string) => { let [hh, mm] = (schedTime.value || '09:00').split(':'); if (kind === 'h') hh = v; else mm = v; schedTime.value = `${hh}:${mm}`; renderLabels(); panel.querySelectorAll(`[data-kind="${kind}"]`).forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('sel', (x as HTMLElement).dataset.v === v)); };
        panel.querySelectorAll('.tm-i').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); setPart((b as HTMLElement).dataset.kind!, (b as HTMLElement).dataset.v!); }));
        requestAnimationFrame(() => { panel.querySelectorAll('.tm-col').forEach((c) => centerIn(c as HTMLElement, c.querySelector('.tm-i.sel'))); });
      };

      // ---- zone (search + list) ----
      const buildTz = (panel: HTMLElement) => {
        const rows = (q: string) => TZ.filter((t) => !q || t.label.toLowerCase().includes(q) || t.z.toLowerCase().includes(q)).map((t) => `<button type="button" class="tz-i${t.z === schedTz.value ? ' sel' : ''}" data-z="${esc(t.z)}"><b>${fmtOff(t.off)}</b><span>${esc(t.z.replace(/_/g, ' '))}</span></button>`).join('');
        panel.innerHTML = `<div class="tz-s"><input type="text" placeholder="Search zone or offset…" data-focus /></div><div class="tz-l">${rows('')}</div>`;
        const list = panel.querySelector('.tz-l') as HTMLElement; const inp = panel.querySelector('input') as HTMLInputElement;
        const bind = () => list.querySelectorAll('.tz-i').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); schedTz.value = (b as HTMLElement).dataset.z!; renderLabels(); closeAll(); }));
        inp.addEventListener('input', () => { list.innerHTML = rows(inp.value.trim().toLowerCase()); bind(); });
        inp.addEventListener('click', (e) => e.stopPropagation());
        inp.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => e.stopPropagation());
        bind();
        requestAnimationFrame(() => centerIn(list, list.querySelector('.tz-i.sel')));
      };

      wire('spw-date', buildDate);
      wire('spw-time', buildTime);
      wire('spw-tz', buildTz);
      renderLabels();
      return {
        close: closeAll,
        setDefault() {
          if (!schedDate.value) { const d = new Date(Date.now() + 24 * 3600 * 1000); schedDate.value = `${d.getFullYear()}-${String(d.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, '0')}-${String(d.getDate()).padStart(2, '0')}`; schedTime.value = '09:00'; renderLabels(); }
        },
      };
    })();

    const setPrimaryLabel = () => { $('pm-publish').textContent = whenChoice === 'later' ? 'Schedule' : (editing ? 'Update' : 'Publish now'); };
    whenpick.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button[data-w]') as HTMLElement | null; if (!b) return;
      whenChoice = b.dataset.w!;
      whenpick.querySelectorAll('.pk').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('on', x === b));
      $('schedbox').classList.toggle('off', whenChoice !== 'later');
      if (whenChoice === 'later') sched.setDefault(); else sched.close();
      setPrimaryLabel();
    });
    // Interpret the picked wall-clock date+time IN THE SELECTED ZONE and return the UTC
    // ISO instant. Standard offset-correction via Intl (handles DST). '' when incomplete.
    const scheduledIso = () => {
      if (whenChoice !== 'later') return '';
      const d = (schedDate.value || '').trim(), t = (schedTime.value || '').trim();
      if (!d || !t) return '';
      const [Y, Mo, Da] = d.split('-').map(Number), [h, mi] = t.split(':').map(Number);
      if ([Y, Mo, Da, h, mi].some((n) => !Number.isFinite(n))) return '';
      const tz = schedTz.value || 'UTC';
      const asUTC = Date.UTC(Y, Mo - 1, Da, h, mi);
      try {
        const parts = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone: tz, year: 'numeric', month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit', hour12: false }).formatToParts(new Date(asUTC));
        const m: any = {}; for (const p of parts) m[p.type] = p.value;
        const tzAsUTC = Date.UTC(+m.year, +m.month - 1, +m.day, (+m.hour) % 24, +m.minute, +m.second);
        return new Date(asUTC - (tzAsUTC - asUTC)).toISOString(); // wall time in tz → UTC
      } catch { return new Date(asUTC).toISOString(); }
    };

    // The mail toggle drives the hidden #pm-email-subs checkbox the engine reads.
    const mailTog = $('pm-mail-tog');
    function syncMailTog() {
      const cb = $('pm-email-subs') as HTMLInputElement;
      mailTog.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(cb.checked));
      mailTog.toggleAttribute('disabled', cb.disabled);
      mailTog.style.opacity = cb.disabled ? '0.45' : '1';
    }
    mailTog.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const cb = $('pm-email-subs') as HTMLInputElement;
      if (cb.disabled) return;
      cb.checked = !cb.checked; syncMailTog();
    });

    // --- Series: a dropdown of the site's existing series (+ "New series…"), a chevron
    // that expands the plate specs, and the name input revealed only when creating one.
    // #pm-series stays the value the publish handler reads — the dropdown just drives it.
    const seriesInput = $('pm-series') as HTMLInputElement; // hidden value store the handler reads
    const specsBtn = $('pm-series-more');
    function syncSeriesUI() {
      const has = !!seriesInput.value.trim();
      specsBtn.classList.toggle('off', !has);
      if (!has) { $('seriesknobs').classList.add('off'); specsBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'); }
    }
    // The series field is now a custom on-brand combobox (matches the schedule pickers):
    // a searchable list of the site's existing series + a "Create …" row for a new one.
    // Same slugify as functions/api/admin/post.js — a series' grouping key.
    const seriesSlugify = (s: string) => String(s).toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '');
    let seriesPosts: any[] = []; // the post catalog, kept so we can suggest the next part number
    const seriesPicker = mountSeriesPicker($('pm-series-pick'), {
      loadNames: async () => {
        const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
        const token = data.session && data.session.access_token;
        if (!token) return [];
        const r = await fetch('/api/admin/posts', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } });
        const d = await r.json();
        seriesPosts = d.posts || [];
        return [...new Set(seriesPosts.map((p: any) => String(p.seriesTitle || p.series || '').trim()).filter(Boolean))].sort() as string[];
      },
      onChange: (name) => {
        seriesInput.value = name;
        // Suggest the next part = (published parts already in this series) + 1, but only
        // when Part is empty — never overwrite a number the author set. Optional/editable.
        const orderEl = $('pm-series-order') as HTMLInputElement;
        if (name && orderEl && !orderEl.value.trim()) {
          // Suggest one past the highest EXISTING part number (drafts included), so we
          // never collide with an already-drafted or out-of-order part.
          const slug = seriesSlugify(name);
          const members = seriesPosts.filter((p: any) => seriesSlugify(String(p.seriesTitle || p.series || '')) === slug);
          const maxOrder = members.reduce((m: number, p: any) => Math.max(m, Number(p.seriesOrder) || 0), 0);
          orderEl.value = String(maxOrder + 1);
        } else if (!name && orderEl) {
          orderEl.value = ''; // clearing the series clears the suggested part
        }
        syncSeriesUI(); refreshSheet();
      },
    });
    function loadSeriesOptions() { seriesPicker.refresh(); }
    specsBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const open = $('seriesknobs').classList.toggle('off') === false;
      specsBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
    });

    const CK = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12.5l5 5L20 6.5"/></svg>';
    const WK = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 4v11"/><path d="M12 19.5v.5"/></svg>';
    function refreshSheet() {
      let words = 0; try { words = countWords(crepe.getMarkdown()); } catch {}
      const read = Math.max(1, Math.round(words / 200));
      const seriesName = $('pm-series').value.trim();
      const order = $('pm-series-order').value.trim();
      const bits = [];
      if (seriesName) bits.push(escHtml(seriesName) + (order ? ' · part ' + escHtml(order) : ''));
      bits.push(words.toLocaleString() + ' words'); bits.push(read + ' min read');
      $('ps-sub').innerHTML = bits.join(' · ');
      try { syncSeriesUI(); } catch {}

      const title = $('pm-post-title').value.trim();
      const desc = $('pm-post-desc').value.trim();
      const slug = ($('pm-slug').textContent || '').trim();
      let target = 0; try { target = parseInt(localStorage.getItem('aysr:target:' + docKey) || '', 10) || 0; } catch {}
      let notes = 0; try { notes = (JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('aysr:notes:' + docKey) || '[]') || []).length; } catch {}
      const items: any[] = [];
      if (!title) items.push({ warn: true, html: '<b>No title yet</b> — the post needs one' });
      if (target && words < target) items.push({ warn: true, html: `<b>${(target - words).toLocaleString()} words short</b> of the ${target.toLocaleString()} you set for this`, a: 'Keep writing' });
      if (notes > 0) items.push({ warn: true, html: `<b>${notes} note${notes === 1 ? '' : 's'} to self</b> — private, never published`, a: 'Jump to it' });
      items.push({ ok: !!desc, html: desc ? `Standfirst written · ${desc.length} characters` : 'No standfirst yet — write one below' });
      items.push({ ok: pubTags.length > 0, html: pubTags.length ? `${pubTags.length} tag${pubTags.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}, all yours` : 'No tags yet' });
      items.push({ ok: !!slug, html: slug ? 'Address set' : 'No address yet' });
      if (seriesName) items.push({ ok: !!order, html: order ? `In “${escHtml(seriesName)}” · part ${escHtml(order)}` : `In “${escHtml(seriesName)}” — set a part number` });
      if (accessChoice === 'paid') items.push({ ok: true, html: 'Paid — a teaser, then pay-what-you-want' });
      $('ps-checklist').innerHTML = items.map((it) => `<li class="${it.warn ? 'warn' : ''}">${it.warn ? WK : CK}<span>${it.html}</span>${it.a ? `<a data-jump>${it.a}</a>` : ''}</li>`).join('');
      const warns = items.filter((it) => it.warn).length;
      $('ps-note').innerHTML = warns ? `<b>${warns} thing${warns === 1 ? '' : 's'} worth a look.</b> Your call — nothing here stops you.` : 'Everything checks out.';
    }
    // The warning links just drop back to the editor.
    $('ps-checklist').addEventListener('click', (e) => { if ((e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[data-jump]')) { e.preventDefault(); closeModal(); } });
    ['pm-post-title', 'pm-post-desc', 'pm-series', 'pm-series-order'].forEach((id) => { const el = $(id); if (el) el.addEventListener('input', refreshSheet); });
    $('pm-slug').addEventListener('input', refreshSheet);

    // Decide which of the two modal views to show. INVARIANT: exactly one of
    // #pm-signin / #pm-form is visible at all times — the card must NEVER render
    // empty (both hidden). Every failure mode below falls back to the sign-in
    // view, so a thrown/hung/blocked session check (corrupt localStorage token, a
    // privacy extension blocking Supabase, an offline refresh, etc.) can only ever
    // land on "Sign in to publish", not a blank card.
    async function refreshAuthView() {
      let signedIn = false;
      try {
        // Guard against a hang: getSession() can await a background token refresh,
        // and if that network call is blocked it never resolves. Cap it so the UI
        // always settles instead of leaving whatever view was up.
        const withTimeout = Promise.race([
          supabase.auth.getSession(),
          new Promise((res) => setTimeout(() => res({ data: { session: null }, __timedOut: true }), 4000)),
        ]);
        const { data } = await withTimeout;
        signedIn = !!(data && data.session && data.session.user);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('[publish] session check failed; falling back to sign-in view', err);
        signedIn = false;
      }
      $('pm-signin').hidden = signedIn;
      $('pm-form').hidden = !signedIn;
      if (signedIn) { try { prefillForm(); updateEmailToggle(); refreshSheet(); loadSeriesOptions(); } catch (err) { console.error('[publish] prefill failed', err); } }
    }
    function prefillForm() {
      if (editing) {
        // Editing an existing post: preserve its identity — lock the slug, restore
        // title/description/tags/draft, and show a heading so it's clearly an edit.
        // Always reflect the CURRENT editor title (its H1), so renaming the post in the
        // editor is caught here; the locked slug keeps this an UPDATE of the same post
        // (never a fork), so it replaces the original.
        $('pm-post-title').value = firstHeading(crepe.getMarkdown()) || editing.title || '';
        if (!$('pm-post-desc').value) $('pm-post-desc').value = editing.description || '';
        $('pm-slug').textContent = editing.slug;
        // Lock the permalink for an existing post: editing it would fork the post into a
        // NEW file (create-not-update) and orphan the original. Publish forces this slug too.
        $('pm-slug').contentEditable = 'false';
        $('pm-slug').style.color = 'var(--muted)';
        // Draft is a hidden flag the FOOTER BUTTONS set (Save draft = on, Publish/Update
        // = off via pointerdown) — not the post's stored state — so it defaults off here.
        // That way the letter toggle reflects the publish path (a draft-save is blocked
        // from emailing by the handler's `!draft` guard regardless).
        $('pm-draft').checked = false;
        $('pm-series').value = editing.series || '';
        seriesPicker.setValue(editing.series || '');
        $('pm-series-order').value = editing.seriesOrder || '';
        $('pm-series-total').value = editing.seriesTotal || '';
        $('pm-series-status').value = editing.seriesStatus || '';
        $('pm-series-planned').value = (editing.seriesPlanned || []).join('\n');
        slugEdited = true; // don't let title edits rewrite an existing post's permalink
        // Reflect the post's current paywall state in the access picker.
        accessChoice = editing.gateable ? 'paid' : 'free';
        accpick.querySelectorAll('.pk').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('on', (x as HTMLElement).dataset.a === accessChoice));
        $('pricebox').classList.toggle('off', accessChoice !== 'paid');
        $('pm-form-title').textContent = 'Update post';
        $('pm-publish').textContent = 'Update';
        renderTags();
        return;
      }
      if (!$('pm-post-title').value) $('pm-post-title').value = firstHeading(crepe.getMarkdown());
      if (!$('pm-slug').textContent.trim()) $('pm-slug').textContent = slugify($('pm-post-title').value);
    }
    // Keep the permalink synced to the title until the author edits it directly.
    $('pm-slug').addEventListener('input', () => { slugEdited = true; });
    $('pm-post-title').addEventListener('input', () => { if (!slugEdited) $('pm-slug').textContent = slugify($('pm-post-title').value); });

    // --- "Email subscribers" toggle -----------------------------------------
    // Opt-in per publish. Labelled with the LIVE confirmed-subscriber count so the
    // author knows exactly who'll get mail, and disabled when there's no one to
    // email or when saving a draft (a draft is never announced).
    const emailChk = $('pm-email-subs');
    const emailLbl = $('pm-email-subs-label');
    async function updateEmailToggle() {
      // NOTE: no longer gated on the draft flag — that's set by the footer button at
      // click time (Save draft vs Publish). The toggle reflects the subscriber count;
      // the publish handler blocks emailing a draft-save via its `!draft` guard. So a
      // reader publishing a post THAT WAS a draft can still send the letter.
      emailChk.disabled = true; // until we know the count
      emailLbl.textContent = 'Send with the letter';
      try { syncMailTog(); } catch {}
      try {
        const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
        const token = data.session && data.session.access_token;
        if (!token) return;
        const r = await fetch('/api/admin/subscribers?limit=1', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } });
        const j = await r.json().catch(() => ({}));
        const n = (j.counts && j.counts.confirmed) || 0;
        if (n > 0) {
          emailChk.disabled = false;
          emailLbl.textContent = 'Send with the letter — ' + n + ' recipient' + (n === 1 ? '' : 's');
        } else {
          emailChk.checked = false;
          emailChk.disabled = true;
          emailLbl.textContent = 'No confirmed subscribers yet';
        }
      } catch {
        // Count unavailable — leave the toggle usable with a generic label; the
        // server re-checks the real list on send, so nothing is lost.
        emailChk.disabled = false;
        emailLbl.textContent = 'Send with the letter';
      }
      try { syncMailTog(); } catch {}
    }
    $('pm-draft').addEventListener('change', updateEmailToggle);

    // Sign-in (one-time; the session persists after).
    $('pm-github').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = 'Redirecting to GitHub…';
      await supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'github', options: { redirectTo: location.href } });
    });
    $('pm-magic').addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const email = $('pm-email').value.trim();
      if (!email) return;
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = 'Sending…';
      const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithOtp({ email, options: { emailRedirectTo: location.href } });
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = error ? ('Error: ' + error.message) : 'Check your inbox for the magic link.';
    });
    supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange(() => { if (!modal.hidden) refreshAuthView(); });

    // Tags as chips.
    const tagInput = $('pm-tag-input');
    function renderTags() {
      $('pm-tags').querySelectorAll('.pm-chip').forEach((c) => c.remove());
      pubTags.forEach((t, i) => {
        const chip = document.createElement('span');
        chip.className = 'pm-chip';
        chip.textContent = t;
        const x = document.createElement('button');
        x.type = 'button';
        x.textContent = '×';
        x.addEventListener('click', () => { pubTags.splice(i, 1); renderTags(); });
        chip.appendChild(x);
        $('pm-tags').insertBefore(chip, tagInput);
      });
      try { refreshSheet(); } catch {}
    }
    tagInput.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if ((e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ',') && tagInput.value.trim()) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const t = tagInput.value.trim().replace(/,+$/, '');
        if (t && !pubTags.includes(t) && pubTags.length < 5) pubTags.push(t);
        tagInput.value = '';
        renderTags();
      } else if (e.key === 'Backspace' && !tagInput.value && pubTags.length) {
        pubTags.pop();
        renderTags();
      }
    });

    // The DB authoring path: save the post into content.posts and publish it via the
    // /api/author/* endpoints (server-bridge → publish_post). The body is rendered with
    // the SAME browser pipeline the file path uses, so the stored body_html is identical;
    // the server adds an inert-guard backstop. A DB publish is synchronous — on success the
    // post is already live at /@handle/slug (no rebuild), so we navigate straight there.
    // `dbPostId` persists the created row's id across saves within a session (so a re-save
    // updates rather than colliding on the unique per-author slug). Seeded from `editing` when
    // reopening an existing post, so the FIRST save targets that post (UPDATE) and preserves its
    // original pub_date. Series/field attach is a later slice — DB posts publish standalone for now.
    let dbPostId = (typeof editing !== 'undefined' && editing && editing.id) ? editing.id : null;
    async function publishToDb({ title, description, slug, body, tags, draft, token, penName, email, series, scheduleAt }, status) {
      status.textContent = 'Saving…';
      let saveJson;
      try {
        const saveRes = await fetch('/api/author/post', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token },
          // Date the post today on first create; on a re-save (dbPostId set) omit it so
          // author_save_post preserves the original pub_date (coalesce).
          body: JSON.stringify({ post_id: dbPostId, slug, title, description, tags, body_md: body, author_byline: penName, pub_date: dbPostId ? undefined : new Date().toISOString(), series }),
        });
        saveJson = await saveRes.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!saveRes.ok || !saveJson.post_id) { status.textContent = (saveJson && saveJson.error) || 'Could not save.'; return; }
      } catch (e) { status.textContent = 'Could not save: ' + ((e && e.message) || e); return; }
      dbPostId = saveJson.post_id;
      // A pure draft (Save as draft) stops here; a SCHEDULED post still renders + is committed
      // with a future publish_at (draft is also set for scheduling, so exclude it here).
      if (draft && !scheduleAt) { status.textContent = 'Draft saved.'; return; }

      status.textContent = 'Rendering…';
      let bodyHtml, bodyText, readingMin;
      try {
        const { renderPostBodyBrowser } = await import('../../lib/render-post-browser.mjs');
        bodyHtml = await renderPostBodyBrowser(body);
        bodyText = bodyHtml.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
        readingMin = Math.max(1, Math.round(bodyText.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length / 200));
      } catch (e) { status.textContent = 'Could not render: ' + ((e && e.message) || e); return; }

      status.textContent = scheduleAt ? 'Scheduling…' : 'Publishing…';
      try {
        const pubRes = await fetch('/api/author/publish', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token },
          body: JSON.stringify({ post_id: dbPostId, body_html: bodyHtml, body_text: bodyText, reading_min: readingMin, email: !!email, title, description, schedule: scheduleAt || undefined }),
        });
        const pj = await pubRes.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!pubRes.ok || (!pj.url && !pj.scheduled)) { status.textContent = (pj && pj.error) || 'Could not publish.'; return; }
        // Scheduled → it isn't live yet, so don't jump to the page; the cron flips it live when due.
        if (pj.scheduled) {
          const when = pj.publish_at ? new Date(pj.publish_at).toLocaleString() : 'the scheduled time';
          status.textContent = 'Scheduled for ' + when + ' — it will go live automatically.';
          return;
        }
        // Reflect the (best-effort) subscriber email in the status before the live-jump.
        if (email && pj.email && typeof pj.email.sent === 'number' && pj.email.sent > 0) {
          status.textContent = 'Published — emailed ' + pj.email.sent + ' subscriber' + (pj.email.sent === 1 ? '' : 's') + '. Opening your page…';
        } else {
          status.textContent = 'Published — opening your page…';
        }
        window.location.href = pj.url;
      } catch (e) { status.textContent = 'Could not ' + (scheduleAt ? 'schedule' : 'publish') + ': ' + ((e && e.message) || e); }
    }

    // Publish.
    $('pm-publish').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const status = $('pm-form-status');
      const title = $('pm-post-title').value.trim();
      const description = $('pm-post-desc').value.trim();
      // When updating, the slug is FIXED to the existing post's; a new post derives it from the field.
      const slug = editing ? editing.slug : slugify($('pm-slug').textContent || title);
      const draft = $('pm-draft').checked;
      // Opt-in per publish; forced off for drafts (you never announce a draft).
      const emailSubs = $('pm-email-subs').checked && !draft;
      if (!title) return void (status.textContent = 'Add a title.');
      if (!description) return void (status.textContent = 'Add a description.');
      if (!slug) return void (status.textContent = 'Need a permalink.');
      // Scheduling: a valid FUTURE time (author_schedule_post stores it; a pg_cron job flips it live).
      const scheduleAt = scheduledIso();
      if (whenChoice === 'later') {
        if (!scheduleAt) return void (status.textContent = 'Pick a date and time to schedule.');
        if (new Date(scheduleAt).getTime() <= Date.now()) return void (status.textContent = 'Choose a time in the future.');
      }
      const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
      const token = data.session && data.session.access_token;
      if (!token) { status.textContent = 'Please sign in again.'; refreshAuthView(); return; }
      // Drop a leading "# Title" from the body so the page <h1> isn't duplicated.
      const body = injectCellOutputs(crepe.getMarkdown().replace(/^#\s+.+\n+/, ''));
      // Series (optional) → { slug, title, order, total, status, planned }; attached to the author's own series.
      const sName = $('pm-series').value.trim();
      const sOrderN = parseInt($('pm-series-order').value, 10);
      const sTotalN = parseInt($('pm-series-total').value, 10);
      const series = sName ? {
        slug: seriesSlugify(sName), title: sName,
        order: Number.isFinite(sOrderN) && sOrderN > 0 ? sOrderN : null,
        total: Number.isFinite(sTotalN) && sTotalN > 0 ? sTotalN : null,
        status: $('pm-series-status').value.trim(),
        planned: $('pm-series-planned').value.split('\n').map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean),
      } : null;
      // THE ONE PUBLISH PATH: into content.posts → live at /@handle/slug (no file, no GitHub, no rebuild).
      $('pm-publish').disabled = true;
      try {
        await publishToDb({ title, description, slug, body, tags: pubTags, draft, token, email: emailSubs, series, scheduleAt: whenChoice === 'later' ? scheduleAt : null }, status);
      } finally {
        $('pm-publish').disabled = false;
      }
    });
  }

  // Boot the editor once we know the visitor is the admin. A returning admin
  // (cached) boots immediately so the studio feels instant; a first-time sign-in
  // boots the moment AdminLayout's check confirms admin. Guarded so we boot once.
  let booted = false;
  function boot() { if (booted) return; booted = true; init(); }
  whenAdmin.then(boot);
  if (cachedAdmin()) boot();
</script>
